    "https://flinders.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/flinders_employment/job/Bedford-Park/Casual-Academic-Register---College-of-Humanities--Arts-and-Social-Sciences_JR0000000090": {
      "title": "Casual Academic Register – College of Humanities, Arts and Social Sciences",
      "description": "Start date: 2024-11-18\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nAbout Flinders Our bold vision, captured in our Strategic Plan: Making a Difference: The 2025 Agenda, is to be internationally recognised as a world leader in research, an innovator in contemporary education, and the source of Australia’s most enterprising graduates. To realise this ambition, we recently made a significant organisational change to a six College structure with a professional staff and services alignment. We recognise the key to our success is exceptional people and we’re seeking an outstanding individual to join the leadership team of our transformed university. Casual Register Flinders University has a number of Casual Registers as a means of expressions of interest for the purpose of casual work, should such opportunities arise. How to Register: Upload your current CV/Resumé detailing your qualifications and experience. You may choose to upload a Cover Letter of no more than 1 page to support your CV/Resumé. Your application will be acknowledged by an automated e-mail once submitted. If a casual opportunity is available and your application is considered suitable, the relevant hiring manager will contact you for a further discussion. Please note, only suitable applicants will be contacted. Applying to the Casual Register does not guarantee employment. Further Information: Pursuant to Child Safety (Prohibited Persons) Act 2016 (SA) this position may be deemed prescribed.  It is an inherent requirement of a prescribed position that the successful candidate maintains a current Working With Children Check which is satisfactory to the University. Please contact Recruitment@Flinders  by email at recruitment@flinders.edu.au  should you have any queries regarding Casual opportunities."
    },
    "https://flinders.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/flinders_employment/job/Tonsley/Cisco-Research-Chair-in-Defence-Capability-and-Security_JR0000017614": {
      "title": "Cisco Research Chair in Defence Capability and Security",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-22\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nFull time\n\nPosition Details Full Time | Five-year contract Academic Level E | AU$217,876 | 17% Superannuation Location: Tonsley / Kaurna Country /Australia View Position Description View Candidate Brochure A Position with Impact: Flinders University is at the frontline of defence-oriented research and is seeking an inaugural Cisco Research Chair in Defence Capability and Security. Based in Adelaide, Australia’s Defence State, and home to some of the nation’s most significant defence projects, investment and sovereign capability development, this is a nationally significant opportunity to lead research at the intersection of digital technology, defence and sovereign capability. With direct access to Cisco’s technology and global research network, you will be positioned at the centre of an environment where Defence, industry, technology and government are actively shaping Australia’s future capability.   Working in partnership with Cisco, the Australian Defence Force, the Department of Defence and Australia’s sovereign defence industry, you will establish and lead an applied research programme that translates emerging technologies into real-world defence capability. You will have the opportunity to shape research that advances AUKUS priorities, strengthens critical infrastructure resilience and builds Australia’s sovereign defence capability.   In this position, you will: Lead with impact: Establish and shape a high-profile applied research programme spanning AI, autonomous systems, advanced manufacturing and/or cyber security, translating emerging technology into capability for Defence and industry. Work at the forefront of innovation: Partner directly with Cisco, the Australian Defence Force, the Department of Defence and sovereign defence industry, with access to Cisco’s next-generation networking, security, AI and IoT technologies and global research network. Build what comes next: Grow a team of researchers and HDR candidates, attract major research and industry investment, influence national conversations and help develop the sovereign technology capability Australia needs for the future.   This is a flagship academic appointment established under the Flinders-Cisco partnership to advance defence capabilities through world-leading research innovation and impact.     About You: You are an established researcher, technology leader or senior defence practitioner with a strong track record in defence, national security or digital technology.   You will bring: A doctoral qualification in a relevant discipline OR equivalent achievement at a senior practitioner level in defence industries or national security Demonstrated expertise in advanced manufacturing, AI, autonomous systems (maritime) or cyber security for defence. A strong record of research, industry or government-funded programmes and/or competitive funding. The ability to translate technical innovation into real-world capability outcomes. Established networks across Defence, government, industry and/or the broader technology ecosystem. Exceptional communication and leadership skills, with the credibility to engage across technical, Defence, industry and policy environments.   International and domestic candidates are welcome to apply. Eligibility and willingness to obtain an Australian Government security clearance at Negative Vetting Level 1 or higher is highly desirable.   A Partnership Built for Innovation: Flinders University and Cisco have established one of Australia’s leading university-industry partnerships in digital innovation and applied research. Since 2015, the partnership has evolved into an integrated ecosystem spanning world-class research, industry collaboration, student innovation, workforce development and translational impact. Through a complementary national network of Cisco Chairs, Innovation Central Adelaide, and the National Industry Innovation Network (NIIN), the partnership provides a nationally connected innovation ecosystem that accelerates research impact and translation, industry collaboration, talent development and the adoption of new technologies to address complex industry challenges. As the Cisco Research Chair, you will be embedded within this dynamic ecosystem, connecting world-class research with Cisco technology, industry expertise and real-world opportunities to deliver impact in Australia and beyond. Why Flinders University? They say know your place.  We say you've found it right here.   Flinders University was founded on the belief that learning should open minds, celebrate individuality and give people the freedom to pursue their own point of view. That spirit lives on in our community of thinkers, doers and changemakers who challenge convention, and each other, to shape what comes next.   Rising to a challenge is nothing new for Flinders. During our first 60 years, we’ve navigated revolutionary changes in social and cultural norms, and have responded to transformative economic, environmental and technological developments. Through it all, we’ve continued to deliver for our students and community, innovating in learning and research to prepare graduates for the changing world they help create.   Reaching beyond the limits of buildings, borders, and backgrounds, ours is an inclusive culture that believes absolutely in equality and opportunity for all. We don't just accommodate differences; we embrace and celebrate them.   So,  why work at Flinders? Recognised as the top 2% university worldwide, with research income soaring to $133 million in research contracts and grants. 17% Superannuation + salary packaging options Flexible working arrangements Awarded the AHEIA Higher Education Award for Workplace Culture Excellence due to our commitment to wellbeing through our  Thriving@Flinders  staff wellbeing program Wide range of professional development activities and services, including exclusive staff study offers  We embrace diversity and promote equity and inclusion for all students and staff, as shown through our three SAGE Cygnet Awards. Vibrant campus life and amenities including on campus  health care services ,  gym  and  childcare centre (Bedford Park, South Australia Recognised as a Veteran Employer of Choice    Our Commitment to Reconciliation and Indigenous Employment Flinders University is proud to be an organisation that is committed to our Reconciliation Action Plan and Indigenous Workforce Strategy. Our vision is to be a preferred employer for Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples. We are committed to progressing Indigenous advancement in education, research, employment, and wellbeing, and strongly encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples for all Flinders vacancies. Prescribed Conditions for Employment Appointment to this role is conditional on the completion of required pre‑employment checks and declarations, each of which must be satisfactory to the University. This includes a Gender‑Based Violence declaration, in accordance with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender‑Based Violence (2025), and a Nationally Coordinated Criminal History Check. An NCCHC disclosable outcome will not automatically disqualify a candidate from consideration. Each case will be assessed on its individual merits and relevance to the inherent requirements of the role.  How to Apply and Information You are required to submit a CV and a three-page Suitability Statement addressing the key position capabilities of the position description . For more information regarding this position, we strongly encourage you to please conta ct Professor Michael Blumenstein via Cse.operations@flinders.edu.au . Applications to be submitted before 10:00 pm (ACDT) on Wednesday, 21 October 2026. Please note, late applications and applications sent via agencies will not be accepted . At Flinders we embrace and celebrate diversity and encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples, and people of all ages, ethnicities, abilities, sexual orientations, and gender identities. Certification Applications to be submitted before 10.00pm: 21 Oct 2026 At Flinders we embrace and celebrate diversity and encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples, and people of all ages, ethnicities, abilities, sexual orientations, and gender identities. Flinders. Fearless."
    },
    "https://flinders.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/flinders_employment/job/Centre-for-Remote-Health-Alice-Springs/Lecturer-in-Remote-Health--Nursing-_JR0000017148": {
      "title": "Lecturer in Remote Health (Nursing)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-25\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\nPosition Details Fixed Term until 31 December 2027 | Up to full-time hours available (0.6 to 1.0 FTE negotiable) Academic Level B | $115,871 - $137,122 p.a. Location: Alice Springs - Arrernte View Position Description About the Role Join our Rural and Remote Health team as a Lecturer in Remote Health (Nursing), where you will play a key role in preparing and supporting the future health workforce for remote and Indigenous communities. This teaching-focused position contributes to excellence in nursing and remote health education through innovative, student-centred learning experiences. Working within a multidisciplinary team across the Northern Territory, you will deliver high-quality teaching, develop contemporary curriculum, and help equip graduates with the skills and knowledge required to thrive in remote acute and primary healthcare settings. Key responsibilities include: Delivering engaging and innovative teaching across nursing and remote health topics, using contemporary educational practices and technologies to enhance student success. Developing, coordinating and reviewing curriculum and learning materials, including undertaking Topic Coordinator responsibilities as required. Providing academic guidance, mentoring and professional advice to support students' learning, career development and readiness for practice. Building and maintaining strong partnerships with healthcare providers, professional bodies and communities to enhance student learning opportunities and workforce outcomes in rural and remote health.   This position makes a significant contribution to the University’s strategic plan to change 10 million lives, Every One Matters, by 2035, through directly contributing to the strategic driver of Student Centricity. By delivering innovative, high-quality nursing and remote health education, supporting student success, and preparing graduates for impactful careers in remote and Indigenous healthcare settings, the role helps create meaningful outcomes for students, communities and the health workforce.   About You You are a passionate and experienced nursing educator with a commitment to student success and excellence in teaching. Bringing contemporary professional expertise and strong tertiary teaching capability, you thrive in collaborative environments and are motivated by the opportunity to prepare the next generation of health professionals for practice in rural, remote and Indigenous healthcare settings. You combine innovative teaching approaches with outstanding communication and relationship-building skills to create engaging and supportive learning experiences. You have a strong track record of designing and delivering innovative, student-centred learning experiences, including the effective use of online and educational technologies. You possess excellent interpersonal, written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to build effective relationships with students, colleagues, industry partners and community stakeholders. You bring experience in curriculum development, academic quality processes and coordinating teaching activities, alongside an ongoing commitment to professional engagement and continuous improvement.   Flinders Rural and Remote Health NT At Flinders Rural and Remote Health NT , our aim is to be a hub for innovative health research, education, and workforce development across the Northern Territory.  We engage with students, community, and stakeholders to provide critical programs, such as the Northern Territory Medical Program, Paramedicine, Rural Clinical School, and the University Department of Rural Health. Our postgraduate education pathways (Remote Health Practice program), provides workforce development through Indigenous health and clinical skills training, and we have a community driven research program led by researchers committed to improving health outcomes. We work alongside Poche SA+NT focussing on Indigenous leadership capacity development and developing the Indigenous health workforce.  All activities are driven by our values which focus on the long-term and short-term needs of the NT community. Life at Flinders We're transforming and investing in people and facilities to create contemporary, stimulating, and satisfying learning and work environments that reflect our core values of excellence, innovation, courage, and integrity. Flinders is refocusing its strategic priorities with the aim of elevating its performance to be a top ten Australian university, and amongst the top 1% in the world. Reaching beyond the limits of buildings, borders, and backgrounds, ours is an inclusive culture that believes absolutely in equality and opportunity for all. We don't just accommodate differences; we embrace and celebrate them. So,  why work at Flinders? 17% Superannuation + salary packaging options Flexible working arrangements Awarded the AHEIA Higher Education Award for Workplace Culture Excellence due to our commitment to wellbeing through our Thriving@Flinders staff wellbeing program Wide range of professional development activities and services, including exclusive staff study offers  We embrace diversity and promote equity and inclusion for all students and staff, as shown through our three SAGE Cygnet Awards. Recognised as a Veteran Employer of Choice 6 weeks annual leave (Northern Territory)  Our Commitment to Reconciliation and Indigenous Employment Flinders University is proud to be an organisation that is committed to our Reconciliation Action Plan and Indigenous Workforce Strategy. Our vision is to be a preferred employer for Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples.  We are committed to progressing Indigenous advancement in education, research, employment, and wellbeing, and strongly encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples for all Flinders vacancies.   Please see here for our Reconciliation Action Plan   Please see here for our Indigenous Workforce Strategy   Prescribed Conditions for Employment A current Nationally Coordinated Criminal History Check which is satisfactory to the University will be required by Flinders University before the successful applicant can commence in this position. A criminal record will not automatically disqualify a candidate from consideration. Each case will be assessed on its individual merits and relevance to the inherent requirements of the role. Please note that you may be required to provide evidence that you are up to date with COVID-19 vaccinations, in line with the Flinders University  COVID-19 Vaccination Policy   Northern Territory Government legislation (the Care and Protection of Children Act 2007) now requires all individuals in child related employment or whose duties involve, or are likely to involve, contact with a child, to hold a valid 'Working with Children Clearance' (Ochre Card). This position involves child related work and is assessed as requiring a Working with Children Clearance/Ochre Card. A valid Northern Territory (NT) Driver’s License is an essential requirement of this position and must be maintained for the duration of employment. How to Apply and Information You are required to submit a CV, along with a Suitability Statement as a separate document.  This should be no more than 3 pages, and address the Key Position Capabilities of the position description . Flinders University is committed to providing an environment where staff with disability are valued, supported and encouraged, and can, as far as practicably possible, participate fully and independently in the life of the University. If you require any reasonable adjustments to assist you in the selection process, including being accompanied by an accredited assistance animal with public access rights as per the Disability Policy , please advise the contact the Recruitment Team so that we can make appropriate arrangements through recruitment@flinders.edu.au or call 08 8201 2383. For more information regarding this position, please contact Kim Pearce Applications to be submitted before 10:00 pm (ACDT) Sunday, 25 October 2026. Please note, late applications and applications sent via agencies will not be accepted . At Flinders we embrace and celebrate diversity and encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples, and people of all ages, ethnicities, abilities, sexual orientations, and gender identities. Certification Applications to be submitted before 10.00pm: 25 Oct 2026 At Flinders we embrace and celebrate diversity and encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples, and people of all ages, ethnicities, abilities, sexual orientations, and gender identities. Flinders. Fearless."
    },
    "https://flinders.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/flinders_employment/job/Bedford-Park--Kaurna-Country/Senior-Architectural-Lead_JR0000017683": {
      "title": "Senior Architectural Lead",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-30\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\nPosition Details Full-Time | Continuing Higher Education Officer Level 10 | $147,656 - $156,497 Location: Bedford Park / Kaurna Country View Position Description About the Role   This is a unique opportunity to shape the future direction of digital architecture at Flinders University.  As the Senior Architectural Lead, you will play a pivotal role in establishing and leading a newly formed collective architecture function, bringing together multiple architecture disciplines and domains to develop a cohesive and future-focused digital environment for Flinders University.   As a key contributor to the development and delivery of the University's Digital Strategy, you will work closely with university leaders and stakeholders to drive strategic innovation and influence technology direction that support the University's long-term objectives.   Universities are among the most diverse and complex technology environments, providing exposure to a broad range of digital capabilities including enterprise applications, cloud services, infrastructure, cybersecurity, data, research technologies, student systems and emerging digital solutions. This breadth offers an exceptional opportunity to expand your architectural leadership and make an impact across a wide range of initiatives.   As part of the leadership team within Digital Strategy and Innovation, you will help shape the future directions by leading, supporting and driving innovative solutions that deliver meaningful outcomes for students, academics, staff and the wider University community.   Providing strategic and operational leadership to relevant stakeholders and teams within IDS, you will be responsible for developing and maintaining the current and target state enterprise architecture, reference architecture and technology roadmap. The role also focuses on improving the effectiveness, sustainability and cost efficiency of solutions through the identification and replacement of legacy components and the reduction of technical duplication, complexity and inefficiency.   You will work closely with IDS teams to ensure priorities are aligned with the strategic and operational objectives of customers, while leading a team of professional staff and providing strong people leadership and performance management.   A comprehensive list of duties is available from the Position Description   This position makes a significant contribution to the University's strategic plan to \"Changing 10 million lives, Every One Matters\" by 2035, by enabling the delivery of secure, sustainable and future-focused digital architecture and technology solutions that support teaching, research and operations across the University. About You   You have extensive experience building and managing customer relationships within a complex organisation and possess a strong understanding of contemporary agile ways of working, including experience operating within matrix environments. You are recognised for your strategic thinking, business planning capability and growth mindset, and are committed to fostering a culture of continuous improvement, innovation and collaboration.   With high level skills in leading a team to its full potential, including advanced interpersonal and relationship management skills and the ability to manage staff performance, you possess advanced interpersonal influence and demonstrated ability to negotiate and communicate effectively with staff and customers across a diverse organisation particularly during the design, management and implementation of customer solutions.   You exercise advanced strategic thinking, planning and analytical skills that enable you to develop and implement technology strategies aligned with organisational objectives. You bring extensive experience applying contemporary enterprise architecture frameworks within complex environments and have a proven ability to influence, negotiate and communicate effectively with diverse stakeholders to deliver customer-focused technology solutions.   The successful candidate will hold appropriate tertiary qualification in Information Technology or relevant technical area, and / or have equivalent demonstrated experience in a complex IT environment   About Information and Digital Services   Information and Digital Services (IDS) are a pivotal resource of the University, providing information and digital technology services and support to the Flinders University staff and student community. The IDS team apply technical expertise to support university projects and provide core services such as the IDS Service Desk, Audio visual, simulation and event services, Information security and identity access management services and more.    Life at Flinders   They say know your place.  We say you've found it right here.    Flinders University was founded on the belief that learning should open minds, celebrate individuality and give people the freedom to pursue their own point of view. That spirit lives on in our community of thinkers, doers and changemakers who challenge convention, and each other, to shape what comes next.    Rising to a challenge is nothing new for Flinders. During our first 60 years, we’ve navigated revolutionary changes in social and cultural norms, and have responded to transformative economic, environmental and technological developments. Through it all, we’ve continued to deliver for our students and community, innovating in learning and research to prepare graduates for the changing world they help create.    Reaching beyond the limits of buildings, borders, and backgrounds, ours is an inclusive culture that believes absolutely in equality and opportunity for all. We don't just accommodate differences; we embrace and celebrate them.     So,  why work at Flinders?   17% Superannuation + salary packaging options   Flexible working arrangements   Awarded the AHEIA Higher Education Award for Workplace Culture Excellence due to our commitment to wellbeing through our  Thriving@Flinders  staff wellbeing program  Wide range of professional development activities and services, including exclusive staff study offers    We embrace diversity and promote equity and inclusion for all students and staff, as shown through our three SAGE Cygnet Awards.   Vibrant campus life and amenities including on campus  health care services ,  gym  and  childcare centre  (Bedford Park, South Australia).   Recognised as a Veteran Employer of Choice      Our Commitment to Reconciliation and Indigenous Employment   Flinders University is proud to be an organisation that is committed to our Reconciliation Action Plan and Indigenous Workforce Strategy. Our vision is to be a preferred employer for Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples.  We are committed to progressing Indigenous advancement in education, research, employment, and wellbeing, and strongly encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples for all Flinders vacancies.   Please see here for our  Reconciliation Action Plan     Please see here for our  Indigenous Workforce Strategy     Prescribed Conditions for Employment Appointment to this role is conditional on the completion of required pre-employment checks and declarations, each of which must be satisfactory to the University. This includes: A current completed Nationally Coordinated Criminal History Check and Gender Based Violence Declaration which is satisfactory to the University. The contract of Employment is conditional upon the receipt of these completed compliance checks. A disclosable outcome will not automatically disqualify a candidate from consideration. Each case will be assessed on its individual merits and relevance to the inherent requirements of the role.   How to Apply and Information You are required to submit a CV, along with a separate Cover Letter of no more than 3 pages, addressing your suitability for the role, and why you feel you are a good fit. Flinders University is committed to providing an environment where staff with disability are valued, supported and encouraged to participate fully and independently in the life of the University. If you require any reasonable adjustments to assist you in the selection process, please advise the contact in the Recruitment Team so that we can make appropriate arrangements through recruitment@flinders.edu.au or call 08 8201 2383. For more information regarding this position, please contact Karl Sellmann Certification National Police Certificate - Australian Federal Police Applications to be submitted before 10.00pm: 14 Oct 2026 At Flinders we embrace and celebrate diversity and encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples, and people of all ages, ethnicities, abilities, sexual orientations, and gender identities. Flinders. Fearless."
    },
    "https://flinders.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/flinders_employment/job/Bedford-Park--Kaurna-Country/Senior-Lecturer-Lecturer-in-Midwifery_JR0000017694": {
      "title": "Senior Lecturer/Lecturer in Midwifery",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-01\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\nPosition Details Continuing | Full-Time or Part-Time available Academic Level B or C | $115,871 - $162,619 p.a. pro-rata Location: Bedford Park / Kaurna Country View Position Description – Lecturer Teaching Specialist (Clinical Practitioner) View Position Description – Senior Lecturer Teaching Specialist (Clinical Practitioner) About the Role/s Lecturer The Lecturer in Midwifery - Teaching Specialist (Clinical Practitioner), will contribute to excellence in teaching and learning across a range of midwifery topics. The lecturer will play a key role in developing and delivering high-quality, innovative teaching through lectures, tutorials, clinical placements, and contemporary digital strategies. This includes creating course materials, coordinating placements, and conducting assessments. The role also requires ongoing clinical or community-based practice to maintain current skills and knowledge. In addition, the incumbent will provide informal leadership by supporting academic staff, coordinating workflows, and ensuring high standards aligned with university policies and practices. Senior Lecturer The Senior Lecturer in Midwifery – Teaching Specialist (Clinical Practitioner), will provide leadership in delivering excellence in teaching and learning across the suite of Midwifery topics and courses in the College of Healthcare and Enablement, that enhance the student experience. The role will provide educational leadership; curriculum design and review; delivery innovation; advancements in education technologies; and leadership in ensuring internal and external compliance and accreditation of courses and continuous quality improvement of university-level education. The Senior Lecturer will also be expected to concurrently engage in practice in a clinical or community setting to support maintenance of contemporary practice, knowledge and skills. Please refer to the attached position descriptions for a comprehensive list of roles and responsibilities. This position makes a significant contribution to the University’s strategic plan to changing 10 million lives, Every One Matters, by 2035 through a commitment to a student-centred ethos and to developing creative, enterprising, career-ready graduates prepared to become lifelong contributors to society.   About You The Lecturer will have demonstrated excellence in tertiary teaching across classroom, simulation and/or clinical settings, including placement coordination. You will have a proven ability to independently contribute to the development, delivery and evaluation of innovative teaching and learning strategies, including student assessment, and an understanding of the nexus between teaching and learning, research, scholarship and practice. Additionally, as the Senior Lecturer, you will have significant and sustained evidence of excellence in tertiary teaching, including experience in simulation and/or clinical settings. You will have a strong track record of developing, delivering and evaluating innovative teaching and learning strategies across classroom and clinical education environments, together with a demonstrated commitment to teaching scholarship and professional development in higher education. You will have a strong understanding of the nexus between teaching and learning, research, scholarship and practice, together with experience coordinating and/or leading the teaching activities of colleagues. In these roles you will also be able to demonstrate:   A completion of a PhD, or other relevant and equivalent qualification and/or experience. Hold and maintain a current membership with Nursing and Midwifery Board of Australia & Australian Health Practitioner Regulation Agency (AHPRA). Relevant and contemporary clinical experience as an accredited Midwife. An understanding of pedagogical theory and contemporary educational practice relevant to Midwifery. Excellent oral and written communication skills and interpersonal skills, including the demonstrated ability to establish effective relationships with staff, students and industry.     College of Health and Enablement    At the College of Health and Enablement, we aim to be an innovator in contemporary education producing a safer and more resilient health and social care workforce. Our mission is to improve lives and empower communities, enabling better health and caring in the world through an exceptional student learning experience. At the College, our research mission is about co-creating new knowledge which promotes wellbeing, and better care and support, to individuals and communities across the lifespan. We work proactively with industry partners and professional bodies leading to more employable and innovative graduates.      Life at Flinders   They say know your place.  We say you've found it right here. Flinders University was founded on the belief that learning should open minds, celebrate individuality and give people the freedom to pursue their own point of view. That spirit lives on in our community of thinkers, doers and changemakers who challenge convention, and each other, to shape what comes next. Rising to a challenge is nothing new for Flinders. During our first 60 years, we’ve navigated revolutionary changes in social and cultural norms, and have responded to transformative economic, environmental and technological developments. Through it all, we’ve continued to deliver for our students and community, innovating in learning and research to prepare graduates for the changing world they help create. Reaching beyond the limits of buildings, borders, and backgrounds, ours is an inclusive culture that believes absolutely in equality and opportunity for all. We don't just accommodate differences; we embrace and celebrate them. So,   why work at Flinders?   17% Superannuation + salary packaging options Flexible working arrangements Awarded the AHEIA Higher Education Award for Workplace Culture Excellence due to our commitment to wellbeing through our Thriving@Flinders staff wellbeing program Wide range of professional development activities and services, including exclusive staff study offers  We embrace diversity and promote equity and inclusion for all students and staff, as shown through our three SAGE Cygnet Awards. Vibrant campus life and amenities including on campus  health care services ,  gym  and  childcare centre (Bedford Park, South Australia). Recognised as a Veteran Employer of Choice    Our Commitment to Reconciliation and Indigenous Employment   Flinders University is proud to be an organisation that is committed to our Reconciliation Action Plan and Indigenous Workforce Strategy. Our vision is to be a preferred employer for Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples.  We are committed to progressing Indigenous advancement in education, research, employment, and wellbeing, and strongly encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples for all Flinders vacancies.   Please see here for our Reconciliation Action Plan   Please see here for our Indigenous Workforce Strategy      Prescribed Conditions for Employment   Appointment to this role is conditional on the completion of required pre-employment checks and declarations, each of which must be satisfactory to the University. These include:   Flinders University will require a current completed Nationally Coordinated Criminal History Check and Gender Based Violence Declaration which is satisfactory to the University. The contract of Employment is conditional upon the receipt of these completed compliance checks. A disclosable outcome will not automatically disqualify a candidate from consideration. Each case will be assessed on its individual merits and relevance to the inherent requirements of the role. In addition, it is a requirement of this position that the incumbent maintain a current Working with Children Check which is satisfactory to the University in accordance with the Child Safety (Prohibited Persons) Act 2016 (SA). SA: Staff working in a health care setting are strongly recommended to be fully vaccinated against COVID-19 in line with the SA Health policy.    How to Apply and Information You are required to submit a CV, along with a Suitability Statement as a separate document.  This should be no more than 3 pages, and address the Key Position Capabilities of the View Position Description – Lecturer Teaching Specialist (Clinical Practitioner) View Position Description – Senior Lecturer Teaching Specialist (Clinical Practitioner)  Flinders University is committed to providing an environment where staff with disability are valued, supported and encouraged to participate fully and independently in the life of the University. If you require any reasonable adjustments to assist you in the selection process, please advise the contact in the Recruitment Team so that we can make appropriate arrangements through recruitment@flinders.edu.au or call 08 8201 2383. For more information regarding this position, please contact Professor Chris Barr Certification Applications to be submitted before 10.00pm: 22 Oct 2026 At Flinders we embrace and celebrate diversity and encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples, and people of all ages, ethnicities, abilities, sexual orientations, and gender identities. Flinders. Fearless."
    },
    "https://flinders.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/flinders_employment/job/Bedford-Park--Kaurna-Country/Research-Associate-in-Marine-Biology--Biofouling---Molecular-Ecology-_JR0000017701-1": {
      "title": "Research Associate in Marine Biology (Biofouling & Molecular Ecology)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-02\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\nPosition Details Full-Time | Two-year contract Academic Level A | $90,930 - $110,197 pa Location: Bedford Park / Kaurna Country View Position Description About the Role We are seeking an enthusiastic and highly motivated Research Associate to join the ARC Training Centre for Biofilm Research & Innovation (BRIC) and contribute to an exciting research project investigating biofouling communities in Australian waters. Working under the direction of the Chief Investigator and in collaboration with project and partner investigators, you will play a key role in designing, managing and delivering research activities for the project. In this position, your duties will include, but not be limited to: Leading research investigating the establishment of marine biofouling communities on artificial structures. Apply advanced molecular and bioinformatic techniques to assess the diversity, composition, and temporal dynamics of biofouling communities. Design, conduct and analyse experiments examining biofouling processes on marine infrastructure. Contribute to the development of research methodologies, experimental protocols, and sampling strategies to support project objectives. Work collaboratively with an interdisciplinary team of researchers and project partners, including government agencies and industry stakeholders. Interpret and communicate research findings through technical reports, scientific publications, presentations, and stakeholder engagement activities. Assist with project management activities, including planning, data management, reporting, and achievement of project milestones. This position is open to candidates with Australian working rights. Relocation support may be available for the successful candidate. About You You will be passionate about protecting Australia’s marine environments and advancing the sustainable management of its oceans and waterways. You will be a collaborative, proactive and motivated researcher with a strong interest in marine biofouling, molecular ecology or a related field, committed to delivering high-quality, impactful research. As well as completion (or near-completion) of a PhD in Marine Biology or Marine Genomics or Marine Microbiology or Bioinformatics, you should demonstrate; Research experience in biofouling, marine invasive species, marine microbial ecology, or related fields. Knowledge of marine organism identification and taxonomy, particularly in relation to biofouling communities. A growing research profile in marine microbial ecology, molecular ecology, metagenomics, or a closely related discipline, evidenced by publications and other research outputs. Experience applying molecular and microbiological techniques, including genomic and metagenomic approaches, to address ecological research questions. Expertise in bioinformatic analyses and the interpretation of complex biological and ecological datasets. Demonstrated skills in quantitative data analysis, including proficiency in R, Python, MATLAB, or equivalent software. Strong interpersonal and communication skills, with the ability to work effectively both independently and collaboratively within multidisciplinary research teams.   About the ARC Training Centre for Biofilm Research and Innovation  We are the leading Australian research and training centre tackling biofilm-related challenges.   The ARC Training Centre for Biofilm Research and Innovation , led by Flinders University, is a 5 year, $7.8m research and training program, bringing together 5 universities, 10 industry partners and key industry and regulatory bodies to deliver innovative research and biofilm solutions to tackle important issues for the maritime and water industries.  Biofilms grow on all surfaces and environments, from catheters to drinking water pipes and ships. They are complex organisations of cells that grow on both living and inert surfaces and are both viscous and elastic in nature. They can be made up of a single species or comprise several species of different types of microorganisms, including those that pose a threat to either human health or our environment. Biofilm attachment and development cannot be prevented completely thus they cost billions each year to those attempting to eradicate them.    By working with industries to develop innovative solutions that meet their needs and alleviate their biofilm-related problems, the ARC Training Centre for Biofilm Research and Innovation aims to: transform biofouling management strategies for maritime platforms; train the next generation of interdisciplinary scientists and engineers; and to develop biofilm management strategies across the defence and water industries to address evolving regulatory stringency.  Life at Flinders They say know your place.  We say you've found it right here. Flinders University was founded on the belief that learning should open minds, celebrate individuality and give people the freedom to pursue their own point of view. That spirit lives on in our community of thinkers, doers and changemakers who challenge convention, and each other, to shape what comes next. Rising to a challenge is nothing new for Flinders. During our first 60 years, we’ve navigated revolutionary changes in social and cultural norms, and have responded to transformative economic, environmental and technological developments. Through it all, we’ve continued to deliver for our students and community, innovating in learning and research to prepare graduates for the changing world they help create. Reaching beyond the limits of buildings, borders, and backgrounds, ours is an inclusive culture that believes absolutely in equality and opportunity for all. We don't just accommodate differences; we embrace and celebrate them.   So,   why work at Flinders?   17% Superannuation + salary packaging options Flexible working arrangements Awarded the AHEIA Higher Education Award for Workplace Culture Excellence due to our commitment to wellbeing through our Thriving@Flinders staff wellbeing program Wide range of professional development activities and services, including exclusive staff study offers  We embrace diversity and promote equity and inclusion for all students and staff, as shown through our three SAGE Cygnet Awards. Vibrant campus life and amenities including on campus  health care services ,  gym  and  childcare centre (Bedford Park, South Australia).   Prescribed Conditions for Employment Appointment to this role is conditional on the completion of required pre-employment checks and declarations, each of which must be satisfactory to the University.   These include: Flinders University will require a current completed Nationally Coordinated Criminal History Check and Gender Based Violence Declaration which is satisfactory to the University. The contract of Employment is conditional upon the receipt of these completed compliance checks. A disclosable outcome will not automatically disqualify a candidate from consideration. Each case will be assessed on its individual merits and relevance to the inherent requirements of the role. The successful candidate will be required to obtain a baseline Security Clearance.     How to Apply and Information You are required to submit a CV, along with a Suitability Statement as a separate document.  This should be no more than 3 pages, and address the Key Position Capabilities of the position description . For more information regarding this position, please contact the Recruitment team via email at For more information regarding this position, please contact the Recruitment team via email at For more information regarding this position, please contact the Recruitment team via email at recruitment@flinders.edu.au or phone (08) 8201 2383.   Applications to be submitted before 10:00 pm (ACDT) on Sunday, 25 October 2026. Please note, late applications and applications sent via agencies will not be accepted . At Flinders we embrace and celebrate diversity and encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples, and people of all ages, ethnicities, abilities, sexual orientations, and gender identities. Certification Applications to be submitted before 10.00pm: 25 Oct 2026 At Flinders we embrace and celebrate diversity and encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples, and people of all ages, ethnicities, abilities, sexual orientations, and gender identities. Flinders. Fearless."
    },
    "https://flinders.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/flinders_employment/job/Bedford-Park--Kaurna-Country/Social-Media-Officer_JR0000017752": {
      "title": "Social Media Officer",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-12\nPosted: Posted Today\nPart time\n\nPart-Time at 0.5 FTE | Fixed term (12 months)  Higher Education Officer Level 5 | $84,599 - $93,366 (pro-rata) Location: Bedford Park / Kaurna Country   View Position Description     This is a unique opportunity for someone who possess native-level written and spoken communication skills in Mandarin Chinese and advanced English communication skills to work with Flinders Marketing and Student Recruitment Team.   About the Role   Ready to create content that reaches and inspires future students across one of China's most popular social media platforms? As the Social Media Officer (Chinese Channels), you'll help grow Flinders University's presence in China through engaging content, online community building, and digital campaigns that connect with prospective students.   In this role, you will be responsible for: Creating and sharing engaging content across Chinese social media channels, with a strong focus on Xiaohongshu (RED). Building and maintaining active online communities by responding to audiences and encouraging engagement. Tracking social media performance and using insights to improve content and grow audiences. Collaborating with colleagues across the University to showcase student stories and support international student recruitment.   For more information on the key position responsibilities, please see the position description   This position makes a significant contribution to the University’s strategic plan, “Changing 10 million lives, Every One Matters” by 2035, by building awareness of Flinders University among prospective students in China through engaging social media content. The role supports Flinders’ commitment to being student-centred, fostering a vibrant culture through storytelling, and driving innovation through the effective use of digital and social media platforms.   About You   You are a creative and motivated social media professional who understands Chinese social media and what audiences enjoy seeing online. You can create great content, build engagement, and use data to improve results.   To succeed in this role, you will have: Experience creating high-quality social media content, including videos, photography and written posts. Strong understanding of Chinese social media platforms, particularly Xiaohongshu (RED), trends and audience interests. Native-level written and spoken communication skills in both Mandarin Chinese and English. Ability to review social media results, identifying opportunities for improvement and managing multiple tasks effectively.   About the Marketing and Student Recruitment team    The Marketing and Student Recruitment team is evolving in 2026 with exciting new opportunities at our vibrant Bedford Park campus and the cutting-edge Flinders City Campus. As we accelerate our growth ambitions, we are looking for skilled and motivated team members to help drive our marketing strategies and initiatives. If you are passionate about shaping impactful marketing campaigns, building the Flinders University brand, and contributing to the recruitment of future students, we want to hear from you.   Join us in a team that is focused on innovation, excellence, and delivering results that will position Flinders as a leader in higher education.    Life at Flinders      They say know your place.  We say you've found it right here.    Flinders University was founded on the belief that learning should open minds, celebrate individuality and give people the freedom to pursue their own point of view. That spirit lives on in our community of thinkers, doers and changemakers who challenge convention, and each other, to shape what comes next.    Rising to a challenge is nothing new for Flinders. During our first 60 years, we’ve navigated revolutionary changes in social and cultural norms, and have responded to transformative economic, environmental and technological developments. Through it all, we’ve continued to deliver for our students and community, innovating in learning and research to prepare graduates for the changing world they help create.    Reaching beyond the limits of buildings, borders, and backgrounds, ours is an inclusive culture that believes absolutely in equality and opportunity for all. We don't just accommodate differences; we embrace and celebrate them.     So,  why work at Flinders?   17% Superannuation + salary packaging options   Flexible working arrangements   Awarded the AHEIA Higher Education Award for Workplace Culture Excellence due to our commitment to wellbeing through our  Thriving@Flinders  staff wellbeing program  Wide range of professional development activities and services, including exclusive staff study offers    We embrace diversity and promote equity and inclusion for all students and staff, as shown through our three SAGE Cygnet Awards.   Vibrant campus life and amenities including on campus  health care services ,  gym  and  childcare centre  (Bedford Park, South Australia).   Recognised as a Veteran Employer of Choice      Our Commitment to Reconciliation and Indigenous Employment   Flinders University is proud to be an organisation that is committed to our Reconciliation Action Plan and Indigenous Workforce Strategy. Our vision is to be a preferred employer for Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples.  We are committed to progressing Indigenous advancement in education, research, employment, and wellbeing, and strongly encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples for all Flinders vacancies.   Please see here for our  Reconciliation Action Plan     Please see here for our  Indigenous Workforce Strategy        Prescribed Conditions for Employment   Appointment to this role is conditional on the completion of required pre-employment checks and declarations, each of which must be satisfactory to the University.  This includes: A current completed Nationally Coordinated Criminal History Check and Gender Based Violence Declaration which is satisfactory to the University. The contract of Employment is conditional upon the receipt of these completed compliance checks. A disclosable outcome will not automatically disqualify a candidate from consideration. Each case will be assessed on its individual merits and relevance to the inherent requirements of the role.     How to Apply and Information   You are required to submit a CV, along with a Cover Letter as a separate document, telling us a little about yourself, and why you feel you are suited to this role. Flinders University is committed to providing an environment where staff with disability are valued, supported and encouraged to participate fully and independently in the life of the University. If you require any reasonable adjustments to assist you in the selection process, please advise the contact in the Recruitment Team so that we can make appropriate arrangements through  recruitment@flinders.edu.au  or call 08 8201 2383.  For more information regarding this position, please contact  Laura Logan   Certification Applications to be submitted before 10.00pm: 25 Oct 2026 At Flinders we embrace and celebrate diversity and encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples, and people of all ages, ethnicities, abilities, sexual orientations, and gender identities. Flinders. Fearless."
    },
    "https://flinders.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/flinders_employment/job/Bedford-Park--Kaurna-Country/Procurement-Category-Manager_JR0000017110": {
      "title": "Procurement Category Manager",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-12\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\nPosition Details   Full-Time | Fixed term (15 months) HEO9 - $133,860 + 17% Super Location: Bedford Park / Kaurna Country View Position Description    About the Role   The Procurement Category Manager at Flinders University is responsible for the procurement and contracting of specified major commodity groups across the University, or for specific high-risk procurement projects.  The role involves developing an in-depth understanding of the University stakeholder requirements including extensive consultation with user groups and leading cross functional teams to deliver exceptional procurement outcomes. This may include being responsible for the creation or review of some or all documentation related to the procurement process and ensuring that appropriate changes and updates are made to Flinders University systems as well as procedures and guidelines. Working in this impactful role will involve: Developing procurement strategies to meet the commercial imperative of the University as well as stakeholder requirements, incorporating overall market approach, proposed contract type, scope and length. Undertaking procurement processes to achieve strategic outcomes, including preparing Acquisition Plans, undertaking market approaches, evaluation and recommendations, and all Governance reporting. Establishing and leading cross functional teams of stakeholders and/or functional experts as appropriate to undertake processes, including evaluations.  Ensuring stakeholders are appropriately engaged and managed. Ensuring project management protocols are maintained, and that appropriate reporting occurs with regards to progress, risks and issues. Please note, due to the nature of the role, you will be required to work from the Bedford Park campus. About You   We are looking for a skilled and personable procurement professional with: Experience in the development of procurement documentation including approvals documentation and market approach documentation. Well developed commercial sense, including negotiation of contracts and the drafting of contracts High level oral, written and interpersonal communication skills including being an effective listener and negotiator, being able to ask clear questions about issues and requirements, and experience in writing quality reports and recommendations for complex and sensitive issues. Proficiency in the identification, development and implementation of procurement strategies for a range of category groups or specific projects Demonstrated experience of managing a complex end to end procurement process from identification of customer needs through to contract execution and contract handover. About Finance and Procurement Services  Finance and Procurement Services assist the University to achieve its goals by providing quality leadership, information, and financial services. The Finance and Procurement Services team undertakes monthly financial management reporting and forecasting, annual budgets and monitoring performance against these budgets, all regulatory financial reporting, monthly compliance, procurement contracting and functional areas of paying suppliers, receipting revenue and annual financial statements.  While this role is based at Bedford Park, we have team members located across all of Flinders sites. Life at Flinders We're transforming and investing in people and facilities to create contemporary, stimulating, and satisfying learning and work environments that reflect our core values of excellence, innovation, courage, and integrity. Flinders is refocusing its strategic priorities with the aim of elevating its performance to be a top ten Australian university, and amongst the top 1% in the world. Reaching beyond the limits of buildings, borders, and backgrounds, ours is an inclusive culture that believes absolutely in equality and opportunity for all. We don't just accommodate differences; we embrace and celebrate them. So,  why work at Flinders? 17% Superannuation + salary packaging options   Our commitment to wellbeing through our Thriving@Flinders initiative  Wide range of professional development activities and services, including exclusive staff study offers    We embrace diversity and promote equity and inclusion for all students and staff, as shown through our three SAGE Cygnet Awards.   Vibrant campus life and amenities including on campus  health care services ,  gym  and  childcare centre (Bedford Park, South Australia).   Our Commitment to Reconciliation and Indigenous Employment   Flinders University is proud to be an organisation that is committed to our Reconciliation Action Plan and Indigenous Workforce Strategy. Our vision is to be a preferred employer for Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples.  We are committed to progressing Indigenous advancement in education, research, employment, and wellbeing, and strongly encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples for all Flinders vacancies.  Please see here for our Reconciliation Action Plan    Please see here for our Indigenous Workforce Strategy   Prescribed Conditions for Employment A current Nationally Coordinated Criminal History Check which is satisfactory to the University will be required by Flinders University before the successful applicant can commence in this position . A criminal record will not automatically disqualify a candidate from consideration. Each case will be assessed on its individual merits and relevance to the inherent requirements of the role.   How to Apply and Information   In addition to uploading your CV, please submit a separate Suitability Statement of no more than 3 pages, addressing the key position capabilities of the Position Description. For more information regarding this position, please contact Deborah Ashdown Applications will be considered as they are received. To avoid disappointment, we encourage applicants to submit their application as soon as possible, as we may close the advertisement early should a suitable candidate be identified. If you have previously applied for this position, there is no need to submit another application. Certification Applications to be submitted before 10.00pm: 25 Oct 2026 At Flinders we embrace and celebrate diversity and encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples, and people of all ages, ethnicities, abilities, sexual orientations, and gender identities. Flinders. Fearless."
    },
    "https://flinders.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/flinders_employment/job/Bedford-Park--Kaurna-Country/Senior-Network-Services-Officer_JR0000017747": {
      "title": "Senior Network Services Officer",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-12\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\nPosition Details Full-Time | Continuing Higher Education Officer Level 6 | $94,456 - $100,710 Location: Bedford Park / Kaurna Country View Position Description   About the Role We're looking for someone with a strong foundation in networking who is curious, adaptable, and enjoys being part of a team.   While experience is valued, attitude is paramount. We want someone who is keen to learn, willing to get involved across infrastructure and technology domains when needed, and comfortable rolling up their sleeves to solve problems wherever they arise. This role is ideal for someone who sees every challenge as an opportunity to learn, improve, and contribute.   The Network Engineer plays a key role in the delivery, support, and continuous improvement of the University's network infrastructure and connectivity services. Working within the Cloud & Infrastructure Services team, you will help maintain reliable, secure, and scalable network services that support teaching, learning, research, and business operations across the University.   This is a hands-on technical role that will suit an engineer who enjoys solving problems, working collaboratively, and contributing beyond their core area of expertise when required.   As the Senior Network Services Officer, you will be responsible for: Supporting the delivery, management and continuous improvement of the University's network services and infrastructure. Contributing to the implementation of network technology strategies, projects and roadmap initiatives. Partnering with stakeholders to provide technical expertise and enhance customer-focused network services. Identifying and mitigating risks, while monitoring emerging technologies and supporting best-practice network operations.   A more comprehensive list of duties is available from the Position Description   This position makes a significant contribution to the University’s strategic plan to “Changing 10 million lives, Every One Matters”, by 2035 through the delivery of secure, reliable and future-focused network services that enable teaching, research and operations across the University. The role supports a culture of innovation, continuous improvement and agile ways of working to meet evolving technology and business needs.   About You   To be successful in this role, you will demonstrate: Relevant qualifications in Information Technology (or a related discipline) and/or equivalent experience in a technical IT environment. Experience in one or more areas including routing protocols, network troubleshooting, switching architectures, network security, firewalls, VPNs or multi-vendor network environments. Strong analytical, planning and problem-solving skills, with the ability to identify and deliver effective technical solutions. Excellent communication and stakeholder engagement skills, coupled with experience working collaboratively in agile or matrix-based environments.   Experience within the higher education sector and/or Cisco networking environments, including CCNA certification or equivalent experience, will be highly regarded.   What We're Looking For   You are a technically capable network professional with strong analytical and problem-solving skills, a customer-focused approach and a genuine desire to continuously develop your expertise. You enjoy working collaboratively, building effective relationships with stakeholders and contributing to the delivery of reliable, high-quality technology services.   Why Join the Team?   We're building a team of people who are collaborative, adaptable, and willing to help wherever needed. While networking is the primary focus of this role, we are looking for someone who understands that delivering great technology outcomes is a team sport.   If you're the type of person who enjoys learning, isn't afraid to step outside your comfort zone, and wants exposure to a broad range of infrastructure technologies, we'd love to hear from you.   Technical skills can be learned. Curiosity, initiative, teamwork, and attitude are what make great engineers. Opportunity to work with modern cloud, network, and security technologies   What Success Looks Like   After 12 months in this role, you will have: Become a trusted member of the Infrastructure Services team. Built a strong understanding of the University's network and technology environment. Contributed to service improvements and infrastructure projects. Developed skills beyond traditional networking into cloud, security, and platform technologies. Established strong working relationships across IDS and the broader University.   This is an excellent opportunity for a network engineer who wants more than \"just networking\" and is looking to grow into a well-rounded infrastructure professional   Life at Flinders   They say know your place.  We say you've found it right here.  Flinders University was founded on the belief that learning should open minds, celebrate individuality and give people the freedom to pursue their own point of view. That spirit lives on in our community of thinkers, doers and changemakers who challenge convention, and each other, to shape what comes next.  Rising to a challenge is nothing new for Flinders. During our first 60 years, we’ve navigated revolutionary changes in social and cultural norms, and have responded to transformative economic, environmental and technological developments. Through it all, we’ve continued to deliver for our students and community, innovating in learning and research to prepare graduates for the changing world they help create.  Reaching beyond the limits of buildings, borders, and backgrounds, ours is an inclusive culture that believes absolutely in equality and opportunity for all. We don't just accommodate differences; we embrace and celebrate them.     Our Commitment to Reconciliation and Indigenous Employment   Flinders University is proud to be an organisation that is committed to our Reconciliation Action Plan and Indigenous Workforce Strategy. Our vision is to be a preferred employer for Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples.  We are committed to progressing Indigenous advancement in education, research, employment, and wellbeing, and strongly encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples for all Flinders vacancies.   Please see here for our  Reconciliation Action Plan     Please see here for our  Indigenous Workforce Strategy       Prescribed Conditions for Employment   Appointment to this role is conditional on the completion of required pre-employment checks and declarations, each of which must be satisfactory to the University. This includes: A current completed Nationally Coordinated Criminal History Check and Gender Based Violence Declaration which is satisfactory to the University. The contract of Employment is conditional upon the receipt of these completed compliance checks. A disclosable outcome will not automatically disqualify a candidate from consideration. Each case will be assessed on its individual merits and relevance to the inherent requirements of the role.   How to Apply and Information You are required to submit a CV, along with a Suitability Statement of no more than 3 pages, addressing the below Key Position Capabilities of the Position Description : Well-developed thinking, planning and analytical skills. Well-developed self-improvement and growth mindset/approach to the role and as part of a wider team. Well-developed interpersonal influence and demonstrated ability to negotiate and communicate effectively with staff and customers across a diverse organisation particularly during the design, management and implementation of customer solutions. Cisco Certified Network Associate (CCNA) certification or demonstrated experience in configuring or managing a CISCO Environment. Well-developed experience in at least one of current routing protocols, network troubleshooting techniques, a multi-vendor/multi-protocol environment, modern switching architectures, structured cabling standards and network security environments, including but not limited to firewalls and VPNs. Flinders University is committed to providing an environment where staff with disability are valued, supported and encouraged to participate fully and independently in the life of the University. If you require any reasonable adjustments to assist you in the selection process, please advise the contact in the Recruitment Team so that we can make appropriate arrangements through recruitment@flinders.edu.au or call 08 8201 2383. For more information regarding this position, please contact Warren Pearse Certification National Police Certificate - Australian Federal Police Applications to be submitted before 10.00pm: 25 Oct 2026 At Flinders we embrace and celebrate diversity and encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples, and people of all ages, ethnicities, abilities, sexual orientations, and gender identities. Flinders. Fearless."
    },
    "https://flinders.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/flinders_employment/job/Bedford-Park--Kaurna-Country/HDR-Engagement-Senior-Support-Officer_JR0000017724": {
      "title": "HDR Engagement Senior Support Officer",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-07\nPosted: Posted 5 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nPosition Details 5-Years Fixed Term I Full Time Higher Education Officer Level 6 I $94,456 - $100,710 + 17% Super Location: Bedford Park / Kaurna Country View Position Description A Role with Impact: The HDR Engagement Senior Support Officer is a key role within the Office of Graduate Research (OGR), providing high-level administrative, project and stakeholder support for national and international Higher Degree by Research (HDR) engagement and partnership activities.   Working closely with the Dean of Graduate Research, HDR Strategic Operations and Quality Assurance Partner, College HDR Coordinators and the HDR Engagement and Partnerships Manager, you will support initiatives including cotutelle arrangements, industry internships, scholarships and the National Industry PhD Program. You will coordinate projects, reporting, committees and events while providing advice and support to HDR students, supervisors and internal and external stakeholders.   The HDR Engagement Senior Support Officer will: Support HDR engagement and partnership initiatives, including cotutelles, internships, industry scholarships and the National Industry PhD Program. Coordinate projects, reporting, committees and events that support national and international HDR engagement and partnership activities. Provide advice and high-quality support to HDR students, supervisors and stakeholders on relevant policies, procedures and engagement opportunities. Build strong relationships and contribute to continuous improvement, working across Colleges, professional services and external industry partners to enhance HDR engagement and services   About You You are an organised, collaborative and highly capable professional with experience providing administrative, project or coordination support, ideally within the higher education sector.   You bring strong attention to detail, excellent communication skills and the ability to manage multiple priorities while delivering high-quality outcomes. You are confident interpreting policies and procedures, working with a diverse range of stakeholders and providing professional advice and support in a complex environment.   You demonstrate: Experience providing high-level administrative, project or coordination support, preferably within higher education, research partnerships or industry engagement. The ability to interpret, apply and provide advice on complex policies, procedures and guidelines, with strong attention to detail and accuracy. Experience working with databases and complex information systems, together with strong Microsoft Office skills. An understanding of current issues affecting the higher education sector, particularly HDR engagement, research partnerships and industry collaboration.   About the Office of Graduate Research: The Office of Graduate Research (OGR) supports the success, development and impact of Flinders University’s Higher Degree by Research (HDR) community. Our experienced team provides expert support across the HDR lifecycle, from admissions, progression and examination through to research training, employability, industry engagement, international opportunities and supervisor development. We are committed to creating an exceptional HDR experience, fostering research excellence and connecting our researchers with opportunities to make a meaningful impact.   Life at Flinders They say know your place.  We say you've found it right here. Flinders University was founded on the belief that learning should open minds, celebrate individuality and give people the freedom to pursue their own point of view. That spirit lives on in our community of thinkers, doers and changemakers who challenge convention, and each other, to shape what comes next. Reaching beyond the limits of buildings, borders, and backgrounds, ours is an inclusive culture that believes absolutely in equality and opportunity for all. We don't just accommodate differences; we embrace and celebrate them. So,  why work at Flinders? 17% Superannuation + salary packaging options Flexible working arrangements Awarded the AHEIA Higher Education Award for Workplace Culture Excellence due to our commitment to wellbeing through our  Thriving@Flinders  staff wellbeing program Wide range of professional development activities and services, including exclusive staff study offers  We embrace diversity and promote equity and inclusion for all students and staff, as shown through our three SAGE Cygnet Awards. Vibrant campus life and amenities including on campus  health care services ,  gym  and  childcare centre (Bedford Park, South Australia). Recognised as a Veteran Employer of Choice  Our Commitment to Reconciliation and Indigenous Employment Flinders University is proud to be an organisation that is committed to our Reconciliation Action Plan and Indigenous Workforce Strategy. Our vision is to be a preferred employer for Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples.  We are committed to progressing Indigenous advancement in education, research, employment, and wellbeing, and strongly encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples for all Flinders vacancies. Please see here for our Reconciliation Action Plan Please see here for our Indigenous Workforce Strategy Prescribed Conditions for Employment A current Nationally Coordinated Criminal History Check which is satisfactory to the University will be required by Flinders University before the successful applicant can commence in this position. A criminal record will not automatically disqualify a candidate from consideration. Each case will be assessed on its individual merits and relevance to the inherent requirements of the role.   How to Apply and Information As well as a CV, you are required to submit a Suitability Statement of no more than 3 pages, addressing the below four Key Position Capabilities of the position description : Demonstrated ability to interpret, apply and provide advice on complex policies, procedures and guidelines. Strong attention to detail, accuracy, and demonstrated ability to deliver very high standards of work relating to research partnerships and/or industry engagement. Proficiency in working with a complex database such as a student management information system. Experience and/or a demonstrated understanding of the current issues impacting on the higher education sector, particularly as pertains to HDR engagement and partnership activities. For more information regarding this position, please contact Professor Lucy Lewis . Applications to be submitted before 10:00 pm (ACDT) on Sunday, 25 October 2026. Please note, late applications and applications sent via agencies will not be accepted . At Flinders we embrace and celebrate diversity and encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples, and people of all ages, ethnicities, abilities, sexual orientations, and gender identities. Certification Applications to be submitted before 10.00pm: 25 Oct 2026 At Flinders we embrace and celebrate diversity and encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples, and people of all ages, ethnicities, abilities, sexual orientations, and gender identities. Flinders. Fearless."
    },
    "https://flinders.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/flinders_employment/job/Bedford-Park--Kaurna-Country/Senior-Risk-Audit-Specialist_JR0000017714": {
      "title": "Senior Risk and Audit Specialist",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-06\nPosted: Posted 6 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nPosition Details   Full-Time | Continuing Higher Education Officer Level 8 | $116,349 - $128,806 Location:  Bedford Park / Kaurna Country   View Position Description   About the Role   We are seeking a highly capable Senior Risk and Audit Specialist to join Information and Digital Services (IDS) at Flinders University. Reporting to the Senior Information Security Audit & Risk Lead, you will play a key role in strengthening governance, risk and compliance practices across a complex and evolving digital environment.   Working closely with IDS leaders and stakeholders across the University, you will support the ongoing development and continuous improvement of risk and governance frameworks, policies and processes. You will provide expert guidance on risk, audit and compliance activities, contribute to governance reporting, and help ensure strategic and operational initiatives align with best practice governance standards. This is an excellent opportunity for a governance and risk professional who enjoys influencing outcomes, building strong relationships and driving continuous improvement within a collaborative and forward-thinking team.   Key responsibilities include: Supporting the development and continuous improvement of IDS governance and risk frameworks, policies, processes and standards. Providing advice, reporting and support to governance forums, leadership teams and stakeholders to strengthen risk, audit and compliance outcomes. Collaborating with IDS teams to ensure audit, risk and compliance activities align with operational priorities and strategic objectives. Contributing to the development and management of governance, risk, audit and compliance models that support informed decision-making and prioritisation. Undertaking secretariat responsibilities for key IDS governance committees and coordinating associated actions, communications and initiatives.   For a more comprehensive list of duties, please see the Position Description.   About You   You are an experienced governance, risk or audit professional who enjoys bringing structure, insight and continuous improvement to complex environments. You have a collaborative approach, strong stakeholder engagement skills and the ability to balance strategic thinking with operational delivery. You are motivated by the opportunity to influence positive outcomes and help strengthen governance and risk practices across a large and complex organisation.   To be successful in this role, you will demonstrate: Significant experience in governance, risk, audit or compliance roles within a complex environment. Strong analytical and problem-solving skills, with the ability to identify risks and deliver practical recommendations. Excellent communication and stakeholder management skills, with the ability to influence and build effective working relationships. Experience developing, implementing or supporting governance frameworks, risk management processes and reporting activities. Relevant postgraduate qualifications and/or an equivalent combination of education, training and professional experience.   About Information and Digital Services   Information and Digital Services (IDS) are a pivotal resource of the University, providing information and digital technology services and support to the Flinders University staff and student community. The IDS team apply technical expertise to support university projects and provide core services such as the IDS Service Desk, Audio visual, simulation and event services, Information security and identity access management services and more.   Life at Flinders   They say know your place.  We say you've found it right here.   Flinders University was founded on the belief that learning should open minds, celebrate individuality and give people the freedom to pursue their own point of view. That spirit lives on in our community of thinkers, doers and changemakers who challenge convention, and each other, to shape what comes next.    Rising to a challenge is nothing new for Flinders. During our first 60 years, we’ve navigated revolutionary changes in social and cultural norms, and have responded to transformative economic, environmental and technological developments. Through it all, we’ve continued to deliver for our students and community, innovating in learning and research to prepare graduates for the changing world they help create.    Reaching beyond the limits of buildings, borders, and backgrounds, ours is an inclusive culture that believes absolutely in equality and opportunity for all. We don't just accommodate differences; we embrace and celebrate them.     So,  why work at Flinders?   17% Superannuation + salary packaging options   Flexible working arrangements   Awarded the AHEIA Higher Education Award for Workplace Culture Excellence due to our commitment to wellbeing through our  Thriving@Flinders  staff wellbeing program  Wide range of professional development activities and services, including exclusive staff study offers    We embrace diversity and promote equity and inclusion for all students and staff, as shown through our three SAGE Cygnet Awards.   Vibrant campus life and amenities including on campus  health care services ,  gym  and  childcare centre  (Bedford Park, South Australia).   Recognised as a Veteran Employer of Choice   Our Commitment to Reconciliation and Indigenous Employment      Flinders University is proud to be an organisation that is committed to our Reconciliation Action Plan and Indigenous Workforce Strategy. Our vision is to be a preferred employer for Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples.  We are committed to progressing Indigenous advancement in education, research, employment, and wellbeing, and strongly encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples for all Flinders vacancies.   Please see here for our  Reconciliation Action Plan     Please see here for our  Indigenous Workforce Strategy        Prescribed Conditions for Employment   Appointment to this role is conditional on the completion of required pre-employment checks and declarations, each of which must be satisfactory to the University. This includes: A current completed Nationally Coordinated Criminal History Check and Gender Based Violence Declaration which is satisfactory to the University. The contract of Employment is conditional upon the receipt of these completed compliance checks. A disclosable outcome will not automatically disqualify a candidate from consideration. Each case will be assessed on its individual merits and relevance to the inherent requirements of the role.     How to Apply and Information   You are required to submit a CV, along with a Suitability Statement as a separate document.  This should be no more than 3 pages, and address the Key Position Capabilities of the  position description Flinders University is committed to providing an environment where staff with disability are valued, supported and encouraged to participate fully and independently in the life of the University. If you require any reasonable adjustments to assist you in the selection process, please advise the contact in the Recruitment Team so that we can make appropriate arrangements through  recruitment@flinders.edu.au  or call 08 8201 2383.  For more information regarding this position, please contact  Tristan Bibbo Certification Applications to be submitted before 10.00pm: 20 Oct 2026 At Flinders we embrace and celebrate diversity and encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples, and people of all ages, ethnicities, abilities, sexual orientations, and gender identities. Flinders. Fearless."
    },
    "https://flinders.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/flinders_employment/job/Bedford-Park--Kaurna-Country/Senior-Lecturer-Lecturer-in-Palliative---End-of-Life-Care_JR0000017710": {
      "title": "Senior Lecturer/Lecturer in Palliative & End of Life Care",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-06\nPosted: Posted 6 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nPosition Details Continuing| Full-Time Academic Level B or C | $115,871 - $162,619 p.a. Location: Bedford Park / Kaurna Country View Position Description – Lecturer Teaching Specialist (Clinical Practitioner) View Position Description – Senior Lecturer Teaching Specialist (Clinical Practitioner)   About the Role/s The Lecturer Teaching Specialist (Clinical Practitioner) will contribute to excellence in teaching and learning across the suite of Palliative & End of Life Care topics in the College of Health and Enablement. The incumbent will be responsible for making an independent contribution to teaching and the scholarship of teaching using innovations in teaching practices and technologies to deliver excellence in teaching. You will have the opportunity to develop teaching materials, deliver lectures/tutorials or other innovative teaching and learning strategies, coordinate topics and support assessment work. Another exciting aspect of this role is the opportunity to concurrently engage in practice in a clinical or community setting to support maintenance of contemporary practice, knowledge and skills. The Senior Lecturer Teaching Specialist (Clinical Practitioner) will provide leadership in delivering excellence in teaching and learning across the suite of Palliative and End-of-life Care topics and courses in the College of Healthcare and Enablement, that enhance the student experience. The role will provide educational leadership; curriculum design and review; delivery innovation; advancements in education technologies; and leadership in ensuring internal and external compliance and accreditation of courses and continuous quality improvement of university-level education. The Senior Lecturer will also be expected to concurrently engage in practice in a clinical or community setting to support maintenance of contemporary practice, knowledge and skills. Please refer to the attached position descriptions for a comprehensive list of roles and responsibilities. This position makes a significant contribution to the University’s strategic plan to changing 10 million lives, Every One Matters, by 2035 through a commitment to a student-centred ethos and to developing creative, enterprising, career-ready graduates prepared to become lifelong contributors to society.   About You Lecturer You are passionate about educating the next generation of palliative & end of life care professionals, evident through your track record of clinical leadership, excellence in teaching at a tertiary level, coupled with your contribution to the development, delivery and evaluation of innovative teaching and learning strategies. You also have a good understanding of the nexus between teaching and learning, research, scholarship and practice.   Senior Lecturer You have significant and sustained evidence of excellence in teaching performance at a tertiary level, inclusive of simulation and/or clinical setting, as well as student placement and have experience in coordinating and leading the teaching activities of other staff. You bring a strong understanding of the connection between teaching and learning, research, scholarship and professional practice. You are also able to demonstrate a commitment to enhancing teaching excellence through engagement in teaching and learning strategies, scholarly activities, and ongoing professional development in a higher education teaching.   In this role/s you will also demonstrate:   Completion of a PhD, or other relevant and equivalent qualification and/or experience. Hold and maintain a current membership with a relevant professional association. An understanding of pedagogical theory and contemporary educational practice relevant to Palliative and End of Life Care. Excellent oral and written communication skills and interpersonal skills, including the demonstrated ability to establish effective relationships with staff, students and industry nationally and/or internationally.     College of Health and Enablement    At the College of Health and Enablement, we aim to be an innovator in contemporary education producing a safer and more resilient health and social care workforce. Our mission is to improve lives and empower communities, enabling better health and caring in the world through an exceptional student learning experience. At the College, our research mission is about co-creating new knowledge which promotes wellbeing, and better care and support, to individuals and communities across the lifespan. We work proactively with industry partners and professional bodies leading to more employable and innovative graduates.     Life at Flinders   They say know your place.  We say you've found it right here. Flinders University was founded on the belief that learning should open minds, celebrate individuality and give people the freedom to pursue their own point of view. That spirit lives on in our community of thinkers, doers and changemakers who challenge convention, and each other, to shape what comes next. Rising to a challenge is nothing new for Flinders. During our first 60 years, we’ve navigated revolutionary changes in social and cultural norms, and have responded to transformative economic, environmental and technological developments. Through it all, we’ve continued to deliver for our students and community, innovating in learning and research to prepare graduates for the changing world they help create. Reaching beyond the limits of buildings, borders, and backgrounds, ours is an inclusive culture that believes absolutely in equality and opportunity for all. We don't just accommodate differences; we embrace and celebrate them. So,   why work at Flinders?   17% Superannuation + salary packaging options Flexible working arrangements Awarded the AHEIA Higher Education Award for Workplace Culture Excellence due to our commitment to wellbeing through our Thriving@Flinders staff wellbeing program Wide range of professional development activities and services, including exclusive staff study offers  We embrace diversity and promote equity and inclusion for all students and staff, as shown through our three SAGE Cygnet Awards. Vibrant campus life and amenities including on campus   health care services ,  gym   and   childcare centre (Bedford Park, South Australia). Recognised as a Veteran Employer of Choice    Our Commitment to Reconciliation and Indigenous Employment   Flinders University is proud to be an organisation that is committed to our Reconciliation Action Plan and Indigenous Workforce Strategy. Our vision is to be a preferred employer for Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples.  We are committed to progressing Indigenous advancement in education, research, employment, and wellbeing, and strongly encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples for all Flinders vacancies.   Please see here for our Reconciliation Action Plan   Please see here for our Indigenous Workforce Strategy     Prescribed Conditions for Employment   Appointment to this role is conditional on the completion of required pre-employment checks and declarations, each of which must be satisfactory to the University. These include:   Flinders University will require a current completed Nationally Coordinated Criminal History Check and Gender Based Violence Declaration which is satisfactory to the University. The contract of Employment is conditional upon the receipt of these completed compliance checks. A disclosable outcome will not automatically disqualify a candidate from consideration. Each case will be assessed on its individual merits and relevance to the inherent requirements of the role. In addition, it is a requirement of this position that the incumbent maintain a current Working with Children Check which is satisfactory to the University in accordance with the Child Safety (Prohibited Persons) Act 2016 (SA). SA: Staff working in a health care setting are strongly recommended to be fully vaccinated against COVID-19 in line with the SA Health policy.   How to Apply and Information You are required to submit a CV, along with a Suitability Statement as a separate document.  This should be no more than 3 pages, and address the Key Position Capabilities of the View Position Description – Lecturer Teaching Specialist (Clinical Practitioner) View Position Description – Senior Lecturer Teaching Specialist (Clinical Practitioner) Flinders University is committed to providing an environment where staff with disability are valued, supported and encouraged to participate fully and independently in the life of the University. If you require any reasonable adjustments to assist you in the selection process, please advise the contact in the Recruitment Team so that we can make appropriate arrangements through recruitment@flinders.edu.au or call 08 8201 2383. For more information regarding this position, please contact Professor Chris Barr Certification Applications to be submitted before 10.00pm: 27 Oct 2026 At Flinders we embrace and celebrate diversity and encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples, and people of all ages, ethnicities, abilities, sexual orientations, and gender identities. Flinders. Fearless."
    }
